                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We need something that calls and reconciles this setting over time.  GPus don't store this persistently, and GPUs will very likely not be available at reboot time."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaXidReporting.cpp",
                    "line": 30,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "ack, today this whole flow is kinda broken, as discussed. holding a socket across an endpoint going down and coming backup, the socket won't be functional without re-enumeration and recreating the socket."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaXidReporting.cpp",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "We should take this as a constructor argument so this class can be used for multiple device type and not just GPU. Better to implement event subscription and event handling in separate classes as later is device specific and former is not."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaXidReporting.cpp",
                    "line": 66,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Marc Olberding",
                        "email": "molberding@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "molbear"
                    },
                    "message": "sure. They are separate classes today, but I can move this to the ctor."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaXidReporting.hpp",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "All device type (GPU, PCIe) supports event and hence this can be made device type agnostic (we should not make event subscription GPU specific). We can put this class in a common file related to events (not file specific to xid events)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaXidReporting.hpp",
